-- title:
--   Summed cocycle Φ and its coboundary for [p]_F
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, let $n$ be a natural number and let $F_0$ be an $n$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $k$: an $n$-tuple of power series $F_{0,i}\in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n,Y_1,\dots,Y_n]]$ with zero constant term, with linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each of the two blocks of variables, satisfying the associativity identity, and invariant under interchanging the two blocks. Write $[m]_{F_0}$ for the iterated series defined by $[0]_{F_0}=0$ and $[m+1]_{F_0,i}=F_{0,i}([m]_{F_0},X)$, and let $I$ be the ideal of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ generated by the components of $[p]_{F_0}$. Assume $\dim_k\bigl(k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/I\bigr)=p^h$ for some natural number $h$. Let $\Gamma\in k[[X,Y]]$ (in $n+n$ variables) be a symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle for $F_0$, i.e. $\Gamma(0,0)=0$, $\Gamma(Y,X)=\Gamma(X,Y)$ and $\Gamma(F_0(X,Y),Z)+\Gamma(X,Y)=\Gamma(X,F_0(Y,Z))+\Gamma(Y,Z)$. Put $\Phi:=\sum_{i=0}^{p-1}\Gamma([i]_{F_0}X,X)$. Then two assertions hold: first, $\Phi(F_0(X,Y))-\Phi(X)-\Phi(Y)=\Gamma([p]_{F_0}X,[p]_{F_0}Y)$; second, if $\Phi\in I$ then there is $g\in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ with zero constant term such that $\Gamma(X,Y)=g(F_0(X,Y))-g(X)-g(Y)$.
--
--   The two assertions express the $p$-torsion invariant of a symmetric $2$-cocycle, namely the description of multiplication by $p$ on the extension of $F_0$ by the additive formal group with group law $(X,u)+(Y,v)=(F_0(X,Y),u+v+\Gamma(X,Y))$, together with the resulting injectivity statement for $\mathrm{Ext}^1(F_0,\mathbb{G}_a)\to\mathrm{Hom}(F_0[p],\mathbb{G}_a)$ in the finite-height case. It is used in the construction of rigidified symmetric $2$-cocycles for formal groups of finite height and in the study of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_IsSymmTwoCocycle_addCoboundary_sum_subst_nthSeries_eq_and_exists_eq_addCoboundary_of_mem_span.lean

